STEP 3 -- disable port1.0.3 by PATCH                                        FAIL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
host# restconf PATCH OC/config/enabled {"enabled":false}          (14:31:07)
  -> 204 No Content
  RESTCONF after: state still enabled true, admin UP. The OC config read no longer shows
  an `enabled` leaf (before: enabled true).
  DUT: "port1.0.3 admin up running", no `shutdown`, no NSM line. 4050: running, no new line.
host# restconf PATCH IE {"ietf-interfaces:interface":[{"name":"port1.0.3","enabled":false}]}   (14:31:35)
  -> 404 "uri path not found", error-tag invalid-value
  DUT and 4050: unchanged, port up.
  => STEP 3 FAIL: PATCH is the RESTCONF method to merge a change. On the leaf it answered
     204, which means the change was made, but the port stayed up. On the list entry it
     answered 404. A client using PATCH cannot disable a port, and in the first form it is
     told it did.

